WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.343
In tutorial 5.5, you'll choose which
keyword gets your weekly pages first,

00:00:11.393 --> 00:00:13.335
and which ones wait for your OK.

00:00:14.365 --> 00:00:18.865
First, each ladder card on your
Pipeline has an Auto and Manual switch.

00:00:18.915 --> 00:00:21.430
Auto writes its pages in your weekly run.

00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:26.669
Manual waits for your OK on
each page, under Needs you.

00:00:26.719 --> 00:00:29.503
Click the other side to
switch a ladder at any time.

00:00:31.348 --> 00:00:34.933
Next, the number shows each
ladder's place in the order.

00:00:34.983 --> 00:00:39.620
Move up and Move down change it, and the
first ones get the weekly pages first.

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:43.879
Then, Pause stops new
pages for one ladder.

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:47.962
Its positions are still checked every
week, and Resume brings it back.

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:52.394
To remove a ladder, open
it and click Delete.

00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:56.280
The window says what is removed and
what is kept, before you confirm.

00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:03.362
Finally, open Pipeline settings. Choose
the mode for new keyword ladders,

00:01:03.412 --> 00:01:06.048
and Change the level of how
much is done on its own.

00:01:07.344 --> 00:01:10.094
Set how many keywords are
written at the same time,

00:01:10.144 --> 00:01:13.569
and when writing stops while
pages wait to be published.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.144
Use the recommended values puts them back.

00:01:16.194 --> 00:01:17.502
Then click Save.

00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:22.171
Now your weekly pages go to the
keywords you care about most,

00:01:22.221 --> 00:01:24.967
and the ones you want to
check first wait for your OK.

00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:31.537
So: switch Auto or Manual, move ladders
up or down, pause or delete one,

00:01:31.587 --> 00:01:33.392
and save your Pipeline settings.

00:01:34.421 --> 00:01:39.146
Your ladders are in order. Next, choose
your autopilot level and your weekday,

00:01:39.196 --> 00:01:41.165
in tutorial 5.6.
